00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:08,574
This video shows a weather card with animated icons. The data picks the icon for each day, and one component plays them all.

2
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:18,582
Our card shows the weather now, and five days ahead. We have three icon files. Let's put them in one object, named by the kind of sky.

3
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:30,447
Sunny, partly, and rain. The forecast data uses the same words.

4
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:34,201
Next, the big icon for the weather right now.

5
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:53,527
Autoplay plays it as the file says, repeating forever. These files were saved at a calm, slow pace.

6
00:00:54,767 --> 00:00:59,521
Now one icon for every day of the forecast, picked by its sky.

7
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:14,687
Each day looks up its file by the word in the data. Five players, from one line of code.

8
00:01:15,933 --> 00:01:23,221
So, the data chooses the file, and one component plays any of them. A new kind of sky is just one more file.
